# Lumonox product context

Lumonox is an opinionated FastAPI-native observability product for solo developers and small backend teams (1-5). It is not a full Grafana/Datadog/Sentry replacement in MVP.

## Core promise

Useful visibility into a FastAPI app in about two minutes, without observability-infra learning overhead.

## Product rule

If a feature requires observability-engineering expertise to use, it does not belong in MVP.

## MVP must answer

What broke, when it broke, and what requests led to it.

## Explicit non-goals (MVP)

Distributed tracing, custom dashboard builder, query language, complex alerting, Kubernetes/multi-cloud integrations, log pipelines, full APM behavior, enterprise permissions/audit logs.

## Dashboard principle

Optimize for fast diagnosis, not configurability. A user should understand the problem on overview in about five seconds.

## Positioning anchor

Assume users refuse to configure observability; prioritize sane defaults and low-friction onboarding.

When scope is ambiguous, prefer **DEVELOPMENT.md** at the repo root as source of truth.

## Rule self-review

When this rule materially guided the task, follow **Rules self-review** in `lumonox-execution.mdc` and apply it to this file.
